{"name":"Biscuit Cream","hex":"#f9ccb7","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"biscuit","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A small, flat, baked good which is either hard and crisp or else soft but firm; a cookie.","A small, usually soft and flaky bread, generally made with baking soda, which is similar in texture to a scone but which is usually not sweet."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fire (pottery) in a kiln, without a ceramic glaze.","To take part in the sport of tubing, riding down a river on an inner tube."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/biscuit"},{"term":"cream","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The butterfat or milkfat part of milk which rises to the top; this part when separated from the remainder.","The liquid separated from milk, possibly with certain other milk products added, and with at least eighteen percent of it milkfat."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Cream-coloured; having a yellowish white colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cream"}],"entries":[{"title":"Biscuit","blocks":[{"text":"A biscuit is a flour-based baked food item. Biscuits are typically hard, flat, and unleavened. They are usually sweet and may be made with sugar, chocolate, icing, jam, ginger, or cinnamon. Savoury biscuits are called crackers or biscuits for cheese."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b4/Bourbon_and_Custard_Cream.jpeg/330px-Bourbon_and_Custard_Cream.jpeg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Biscuit"},{"title":"Cream","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is a dairy product composed of the higher-fat layer skimmed from the top of milk before homogenization. The butterfat, which is less dense, rises to the top and is skimmed off, resulting in gravity cream. The industrial production of cream instead uses centrifugal separators to make separator cream. Cream is often sold in grades defined by their butterfat content. It contains high levels of saturated fat, in ascending proportion from light cream to heavy cream."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg/330px-01_Mmm..._Apple_Crisp_with_Whipped_Cream.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream"},{"title":"Cream (colour)","blocks":[{"text":"Cream is the color of the cream produced by cattle grazing on natural pasture with plants rich in yellow carotenoid pigments, some of which are incorporated into the fresh milk. This gives a yellow tone to otherwise-white milk at higher fat concentrations. Cream is the pastel colour of yellow, much as pink is to red. By mixing yellow and white, cream can be produced."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg/330px-Milk_heavy_cream_B.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cream_(colour)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/BiscuitsAmerican%26British.png/500px-BiscuitsAmerican%26British.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/60/BiscuitsAmerican%26British.png/500px-BiscuitsAmerican%26British.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"North American biscuit (left) and British biscuits of the bourbon variety (right). The North American biscuit is soft and flaky like a scone, whereas the British biscuits are smaller, drier, sweeter, and crunchy like cookies.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABiscuitsAmerican%26British.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8e/Kronborg%27s_ship_biscuit_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Kronborg%27s_ship_biscuit_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign